# oracle (tight twin, tolerance 1e-10): fix qeq/shielded with explicit ReaxFF C H O N chi/eta/gamma (not qfile reaxff, which the engine does not read) and pair reaxff on the 21-atom RDX cell of examples/reaxff/in.reaxff.rdx-shielded (b332f28), tolerance 1e-6 maxiter 100 (f_2 = iterations), 20 NVE steps with nevery 1
# measured max error vs native (relative): thermo 3.3e-12 (v_nqeq skipped), atoms 7.7e-10. v_nqeq still differs by one or more at tolerance 1e-10 (14.5 vs 13 average), so it is skipped.
# checkqeq no: the explicit parameters are a fix, not the reaxff qfile, so the engine cannot attach it to the pair (the charges are the same)
# oracle-inputs: w123q_rdx.data w123q_rdx.control w123q_ffield.reax w123q_rdx_qeq.params
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 atomrel=1e-8 skip=v_nqeq
units real
atom_style charge
boundary p p p
read_data w123q_rdx.data
pair_style reaxff w123q_rdx.control checkqeq no
pair_coeff * * w123q_ffield.reax C H O N
neighbor 2.5 bin
neigh_modify every 10 delay 0 check no
fix 1 all nve
fix 2 all qeq/shielded 1 10.0 1.0e-10 100 w123q_rdx_qeq.params
variable nqeq equal f_2
thermo_style custom step pe evdwl ecoul etotal v_nqeq
thermo_modify format float %.15g
thermo 5
timestep 0.1
velocity all create 300.0 4928459
run 0
run 20
